    amt6p1: "After completing Year 3 of the Animal Production and Veterinary program, students will acquire the following competencies:",
    amt6h: "🌾 Grade 3:",
    amt5p4: "C. Develop research, survey, and project-work skills to foster creativity and professional competence.",
    amt5p3: "B. Apply methods for planning livestock production projects involving monogastric animals, ruminants, and poultry.",
    amt5p2: "A. Techniques in animal feed production and utilization, natural and artificial animal breeding, incubation, poultry farming, and dairy cattle farming.",
    amt5p1: "After completing Year 2 of the Animal Production and Veterinary program, students will acquire the following competencies:",
    amt5h: "🌾 Grade 2:",
    amt4p4: "C. Develop an entrepreneurial mindset for conducting business and managing small-scale agricultural enterprises.",
    amt4p3: "B. Apply integrated crop-livestock farming systems, use farm mechanization and supporting equipment, and carry out workshop activities using modern technical methods.",
    amt4p2: "A. Techniques in general pig farming, management of livestock farm environments, operation and maintenance of farm equipment and tools, animal health care, soil quality improvement and fertilization, mixed farming systems, and basic workshop skills.",
    amt4p1: "After completing the Year 1 Animal Production and Veterinary program, students will acquire the following competencies:",
    amt4h: "🌾 Grade 1:",
    amt3p5: "Internship: This provides students with opportunities to gain experience through practical work and to learn the knowledge and skills required for real job performance. Internship hours are not included in the formal technical education curriculum timetable.",
    amt3p4: "General education subjects include Khmer Literature, Mathematics, Computer Science, Morality and Civic Education, Physical Education and Sports, Biology, and Chemistry. The standardized time allocation is applied consistently for both general education and vocational subjects.Vocational subjects include technical subjects and local vocational subjects. Technical subjects are designed to help students achieve the educational objectives of each specific technical specialization. Local vocational subjects are designed to enable students to gain practical experience in line with local labor market needs. Vocational subjects are organized in a structured table with clear educational objectives for each technical specialization.",
    amt3p3: "The technical education curriculum consists of academic subjects, extracurricular activities, and internships. Academic subjects are divided into general education subjects and vocational subjects.",
    amt3p2: "3.1.1 Curriculum Structure",
    amt3p1: "3.1 Curriculum Organization and Standardized Time Allocation by Level",
    amt3h: "🌿 3. Curriculum Organization and Standardized Time Allocation by Level",
    amt2p5: "3. Lifelong learning: Fostering a love of learning, perseverance, and problem-solving skills enables students to seek employment opportunities and continue learning throughout their lives. Similarly, technical and vocational education at the upper secondary level differs from short-term vocational training.",
    amt2p4: "2. Development of learning content: Knowledge and skills are changing rapidly everywhere. Students do not only study pre-defined knowledge, but must also continue learning. Technical and vocational education at the upper secondary level differs from short-term vocational training.",
    amt2p3: "Technical education is designed for young men and women in general education and technical schools (Grades 10 to 12 / Years 1 to 3). Their working life may last more than 40 years after graduating from school. Learning at this age has a significant impact on their entire lives.",
    amt2p2: "Future orientation is a long-term goal. The function of education is to rebuild social culture, develop the qualifications of the next generation, distribute skilled human resources for various positions in society, and promote social integration.School education cannot be defined within a single semester or academic year. It is a long-term project that extends beyond one generation’s lifetime. Technical education should also be implemented with a future-oriented perspective.",
    amt2p1: "2.1 Future Career Orientation",
    amth: "🌿 2. Career Orientation for the Future",
    amt1p8: "E. Develop skills in survey research, research activities, project work, understanding rural communities, small business management, and a service-oriented mindset.",
    amt1p7: "D. Apply methods for animal disease prevention, livestock production planning, incubation techniques, and the management of poultry hatcheries.",
    amt1p6: "C. Apply modern techniques related to the operation of farm machinery, livestock production equipment, and various fishing equipment.",
    amt1p5: "B. Techniques for Producing Agricultural By-products Using Locally Available Raw Materials.",
    amt1p4: "A. Techniques in Animal Rearing, Animal Breeding, and Animal Health Management.",
    amt1p3: "Upon completing the Animal Husbandry program through this detailed curriculum, students will acquire high-quality knowledge and skills through theoretical study, hands-on practice, educational field visits, internships at farms, research based on real-world situations, and project work conducted through experimentation and observation.",
    amt1p2: "1.2 Expected Professional Competencies After Graduation",
    amt1p1: "The detailed curriculum in Animal Husbandry is designed with the objective of developing students' professional competencies in line with labor market demands. It aims to equip students with the skills and knowledge necessary to work in the agricultural production sector, including fundamental knowledge and technical skills related to livestock raising techniques, the utilization of animal products, and community leadership for sustainable development. The program also encourages lifelong learning and enables students to continue their education throughout their lives.",
    amtt1: "Skills in Animal Husbandry and Veterinary Care",
    amtp1: "We provide high-quality education to develop students' knowledge and skills for the future.",
    amtp2: "Implementation of the Curriculum for Skills in Animal Husbandry and Veterinary Care",
    amtp2h: "🌿 1/ Curriculum Objectives",
