    agc3p2: "after students have completed the Agricultural Skills Curriculum, they will acquire the following competencies:",
    agc3p1: "1.2/ Expected Competencies After Completion of the Program",
    agc3p: "The Agricultural Skills Curriculum is designed with the aim of contributing to the development of technical skills to respond to the needs of the community, labor market in the region, and lifelong learning to meet the demands of employment in the agricultural production sector with basic knowledge, technical knowledge related to crop cultivation, use and processing of agricultural products with ethics, and leading the community to sustainable development.",
    agc3h: "🌿 1. Curriculum Objectives",
    agt2p8: "h. Land classification, soil analysis and organic fertilizer production.",
    agtt2: "🌾 Standard Level 2:",
    agt2p1: "After students have completed the Agricultural Skills Curriculum Year 2, they will acquire the following competencies:",
    agt2p2: "a. Crop cultivation and field management according to traditional and modern techniques, and land and fertilizer use.",
    agt2p3: "b. Cultivation of high-yield crops such as rice, corn, vegetables, and fruits.",
    agt2p4: "c. Selection of seed varieties, seedling cultivation, and methods of preparing seedbeds for rice cultivation.",
    agt2p5: "d. Use of machinery, tractors or boats, water pumps for agricultural production, and use of modern irrigation systems.",
    agt2p6: "e. Creation and use of questionnaires for data collection.",
    agt2p7: "f. Use of communication skills in conducting interviews with other people.",
    agt1p7: "h. Land classification, soil analysis and organic fertilizer production.",
    agt1p6: "e. Use of tools, materials, methods of measurement and arrangement of infrastructure in crop cultivation according to modern techniques.",
    agt1p5: "d. Selection of crop types, techniques in planting crops, methods in harvesting and managing crop products according to technical characteristics.",
    agt1p4: "c. Performing morphological characteristics of crops, soil profiling, seedling cultivation, and planning for income and expenses.",
    agt1p3: "b. Selection of crop varieties, preparation of planting systems, and measures for crop protection.",
    agt1p2: "a. Crop cultivation and field management according to traditional and modern techniques, and land and fertilizer use.",
    agt1p1: "After students have completed the Agricultural Skills Curriculum Year 1, they will acquire the following competencies:",
    agtt1: "🌾 Standard Level 1:",
    agc2p4: "c. Practical training has provided opportunities for students to gain experience through work practice and to learn about knowledge and skills in performing real work. Hours for practical training are not included in the technical education curriculum.",
    agc2p1: "The technical education curriculum consists of: academic subjects, extracurricular activities, and internships. Academic subjects are divided into general knowledge subjects and vocational subjects.",
    agc2p2: "a. General knowledge subjects include Khmer language, English language, mathematics, computer science, ethics and civics, physical education, biology, chemistry, and physics. The allocation of study hours by standard levels for general knowledge subjects is applied similarly to vocational subjects.",
    agc2p3: "b. Vocational subjects include vocational technical subjects and foundation vocational subjects. Vocational technical subjects are organized to help students achieve educational goals according to specific technical skills. Foundation vocational subjects are organized to help students learn practical applications according to labor market demands in the local area. Vocational subjects are organized in a curriculum that aims to educate according to specific technical skills.",
    agc2: "3.1 Curriculum Structure",
    agtt3: "🌿 3. Curriculum Design and Time Allocation by Standard Levels",
    agc1p4: "3. Lifelong Learning: To instill a love for learning, to be able to persevere, to solve problems and to develop the character to run for jobs as well as to continue lifelong learning. Likewise, technical vocational education at the secondary level has a different nature from short-term vocational training.",
    agc1p3: "2. Building the content of education: Knowledge and skills are changing rapidly everywhere. Students not only need to learn the knowledge that is set as a target, but also need to learn general basic knowledge and deeply consider the skills that can help them maintain and increase their value in the future.",
    agcp2: "1. Target Group: Technical education should be tailored for young people and youth in general education and technical schools (grades 1 to 3). Their working life can last more than 40 years after completing their studies from school. Education at this age has an impact on their entire lives.",
    agc1p: "The direction for the future is a long-term goal, and the function of education is to build a new social culture, develop the quality of the next generation of people, distribute people with capabilities for different positions in society, and achieve social integration. It is a project that has a longer duration than a human lifetime. Technical education should also be implemented for the future. The direction towards the future of technical education in Cambodia has three perspectives:",
    agtt1h: "🌿 1. Curriculum Objectives",
    agtt1: "Implementation of Agricultural Skills Curriculum",
